an nfl player arrested new orleans  running back alvin kamara taken into  custody on battery charges after  sunday's pro bowl now the victim in this  case is now out of the hospital victoria  saha has a look into the events that led  up to kamara's arrest  the victim who was identified as darnell  green talked to police from his hospital  bed at sunrise hospital around 6 pm  saturday evening according to an arrest  report greene told police that he was  leaving dre's nightclub on the strip  around 6 30 saturday morning as he was  stepping onto the elevator with a large  group next to him a man later identified  as alvin kamara put his hand on green's  chest stopping him from walking onto the  elevator green then pushed camara's hand  off green tells police he was hit and  kicked by multiple people green was able  to remember camaro's involvement by his  looks and the clothing he was wearing  police say security footage supports  green's accusations on sunday kamara  played in the 2022 pro bowl at allegiant  stadium where he was arrested after the  game the arrest report says camaro was  interviewed by police at the stadium and  he tells police he saw a fight break out  and saw green get punched police say  camaro told them he punched green  several times because he thought he did  something to the group and he was trying  to run away but the report says  surveillance video showed green was not  running away and had just been punched  by one of camaro's friends and camara  immediately attacked him green suffered  an eye injury but has since been  discharged from sunrise hospital  victoria zaha live local now
 

